@[expose] public section

/-!
# Openness of the locus where a sequence is regular in the fibres

Let `R → S` be a finite type ring map whose nonempty fibres `S ⊗_R κ(𝔭)` are all Cohen–Macaulay
and equidimensional of one and the same dimension `d`, and let `f = f₁, …, f_i` be elements of
`S`. This file proves Stacks 00RA: the set of points `𝔮` of `V(f₁, …, f_i)` at which `f₁, …, f_i`
is a regular sequence in the local ring `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` of the fibre through `𝔮` is open in
`V(f₁, …, f_i)`.

The proof is a dimension count, run on `S̄ = S/(f₁, …, f_i)`. Writing `𝔭 = R ∩ 𝔮`,
`A = S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` and `Ā = S̄_𝔮/𝔭S̄_𝔮 = A/(f₁, …, f_i)`, Lemma 00P1 applied to the fibre through `𝔮`
— a finite type algebra over the field `κ(𝔭)` — splits the relative dimensions of Definition
00QD as
`dim_𝔮(S/R) = dim A + trdeg_{κ(𝔭)} κ(𝔮)` and `dim_𝔮(S̄/R) = dim Ā + trdeg_{κ(𝔭)} κ(𝔮)`,
with the *same* transcendence degree, since `A` and `Ā` have the same residue field. The fibre
being equidimensional of dimension `d` gives `dim_𝔮(S/R) ≤ d`, so, cancelling the transcendence
degree, which is finite,

`f₁, …, f_i` regular in `A` `→` `dim Ā + i = dim A` (Lemma 00KW) `→` `dim_𝔮(S̄/R) + i ≤ d`,

and conversely a point where `dim_𝔮(S̄/R) + i ≤ d` has Cohen–Macaulay fibre of dimension `d`
cut down by `i` equations to dimension `d - i`, where Lemma 00R9 makes `f₁, …, f_i` a regular
sequence. So the set of the lemma is the sublevel set `{𝔮 | dim_𝔮(S̄/R) + i ≤ d}` of the relative
dimension of `S̄/R`, which is open by the upper semicontinuity of relative dimension (Lemma
00QH), transported along the homeomorphism `Spec S̄ ≃ V(f₁, …, f_i)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.RegularSequence.FibrewiseLocus.solution`: the statement of Stacks 00RA.

## Implementation notes

The bound is carried as `dim_𝔮(S̄/R) + i ≤ d` in `WithBot ℕ∞` rather than as `dim_𝔮(S̄/R) ≤ d - i`:
with `i > d` the truncated difference `d - i = 0` would make the sublevel set nonempty at every
isolated point of a fibre of `S̄`, while no ring of dimension at most `d` admits a regular sequence
of length `i > d`, so the two forms disagree exactly where the source's integer subtraction is
negative. `Stacks.RegularSequence.FibrewiseLocus.isOpen_setOf_relativeDimensionAt_add_le` reconciles
the two: for `i ≤ d` the two sets agree because relative dimension is never `-∞` (a fibre contains
the point at which it is taken), and for `i > d` the set with the sum is empty.

## References

* [StacksProject 00RA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00RA)
* [StacksProject 00P1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00P1)
* [StacksProject 00P2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00P2)
* [StacksProject 00QD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00QD)
* [StacksProject 00QH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00QH)
* [StacksProject 00R9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00R9)
-/

namespace Stacks.RegularSequence.FibrewiseLocus

open PrimeSpectrum RingTheory.Sequence

/-- The local ring `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` of the fibre of `Spec S → Spec R` through a prime `𝔮` of `S`,
where `𝔭 = R ∩ 𝔮`: the quotient of `Localization.AtPrime 𝔮` by the ideal generated by the image
of `𝔭`. -/
public abbrev fiberLocalRing (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] : Type _ :=
  Localization.AtPrime q ⧸ (q.under R).map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q))

section Arithmetic

/-- Relative dimension is never `-∞`: the fibre through `𝔮` contains `𝔮`, so it is nonempty. -/
public theorem _root_.Algebra.zero_le_relativeDimensionAt (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] : 0 ≤ Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R q := by
  rw [Algebra.relativeDimensionAt]
  obtain ⟨⟨U, hxU, _, hEq⟩, -⟩ := topologicalKrullDimAt_isLeast _
    (⟨(⟨q, ‹_›⟩ : PrimeSpectrum S), rfl⟩ :
      ↥(PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap R S) ⁻¹'
        {PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap R S) ⟨q, ‹_›⟩}))
  rw [hEq, topologicalKrullDim]
  have : Nonempty (TopologicalSpace.IrreducibleCloseds ↥U) :=
    ⟨⟨closure {⟨_, hxU⟩}, isIrreducible_singleton.closure, isClosed_closure⟩⟩
  exact Order.krullDim_nonneg

/-- For `a ≥ 0` in `WithBot ℕ∞` and `i ≤ d` natural numbers, the bound `a + i ≤ d` is the
bound `a ≤ d - i` for the truncated difference. -/
public theorem add_natCast_le_natCast_iff {a : WithBot ℕ∞} (ha : 0 ≤ a) {i d : ℕ}
    (hid : i ≤ d) : a + (i : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞) ↔ a ≤ ((d - i : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  lift a to ℕ∞ using (by rintro rfl; exact absurd ha (by simp)) with b
  induction b using ENat.recTopCoe with
  | top =>
      have hne : ∀ n : ℕ, ((n : WithBot ℕ∞)) ≠ ⊤ := natCast_ne_top_withBot
      refine iff_of_false (fun h ↦ hne d (top_le_iff.mp (le_trans ?_ h)))
        (fun h ↦ hne (d - i) (top_le_iff.mp h))
      exact le_add_of_nonneg_right (by exact_mod_cast Nat.zero_le i)
  | coe n =>
      rw [show ((n : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) = ((n : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) from rfl]
      rw [show ((n : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) + ((i : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) = ((n + i : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) by
        push_cast; ring]
      constructor
      · intro h; exact_mod_cast Nat.le_sub_of_add_le (by exact_mod_cast h)
      · intro h
        have : n ≤ d - i := by exact_mod_cast h
        exact_mod_cast Nat.add_le_of_le_sub hid this

/-- **Cancelling a finite summand on the right in `WithBot ℕ∞`.** The element cancelled must be
neither `⊥` (which absorbs) nor `⊤` (which is not cancellable). -/
public theorem add_right_cancel_of_ne_bot_of_ne_top {a b c : WithBot ℕ∞} (hc : c ≠ ⊥)
    (hct : c ≠ ⊤) (h : a + c = b + c) : a = b := by
  lift c to ℕ∞ using hc with c
  have hct' : c ≠ ⊤ := fun hx => hct (by rw [hx, WithBot.coe_top])
  rcases eq_or_ne a ⊥ with rfl | ha
  · rw [WithBot.bot_add] at h
    rcases eq_or_ne b ⊥ with rfl | hb
    · rfl
    · lift b to ℕ∞ using hb with b
      rw [← WithBot.coe_add] at h
      exact absurd h.symm WithBot.coe_ne_bot
  · lift a to ℕ∞ using ha with a
    rcases eq_or_ne b ⊥ with rfl | hb
    · rw [WithBot.bot_add, ← WithBot.coe_add] at h
      exact absurd h WithBot.coe_ne_bot
    · lift b to ℕ∞ using hb with b
      rw [← WithBot.coe_add, ← WithBot.coe_add, WithBot.coe_inj] at h
      rw [WithBot.coe_inj]
      exact WithTop.add_right_cancel hct' h

/-- **Cancelling a finite summand on the right of an inequality in `WithBot ℕ∞`.** -/
public theorem le_of_add_le_add_right_of_ne_bot_of_ne_top {a b c : WithBot ℕ∞} (hc : c ≠ ⊥)
    (hct : c ≠ ⊤) (h : a + c ≤ b + c) : a ≤ b := by
  lift c to ℕ∞ using hc with c
  have hct' : c ≠ ⊤ := fun hx => hct (by rw [hx, WithBot.coe_top])
  rcases eq_or_ne a ⊥ with rfl | ha
  · exact bot_le
  lift a to ℕ∞ using ha with a
  rcases eq_or_ne b ⊥ with rfl | hb
  · rw [WithBot.bot_add, ← WithBot.coe_add, le_bot_iff] at h
    exact absurd h WithBot.coe_ne_bot
  lift b to ℕ∞ using hb with b
  rw [← WithBot.coe_add, ← WithBot.coe_add, WithBot.coe_le_coe] at h
  rw [WithBot.coe_le_coe]
  exact (WithTop.add_le_add_iff_right hct').mp h

end Arithmetic


/-! ### General facts used along the way -/

section General

/-- **The image of the maximal ideal in a quotient is not a unit.** If `J ≤ 𝔪_L` for a local ring
`L`, then the image in `L ⧸ J` of an element of `𝔪_L` lies in the maximal ideal of `L ⧸ J`. -/
public theorem mk_mem_maximalIdeal_quotient {L : Type*} [CommRing L] [IsLocalRing L]
    {J : Ideal L} [IsLocalRing (L ⧸ J)] (hJ : J ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal L) {y : L}
    (hy : y ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal L) :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk J y ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (L ⧸ J) := by
  rw [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff]
  intro hu
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hu.exists_right_inv
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective b
  have h1 : y * z - 1 ∈ J := by
    refine Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mp ?_
    rw [map_sub, map_mul, map_one, hb, sub_self]
  have h2 : (1 : L) ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal L := by
    have h3 := sub_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_right z _ hy) (hJ h1)
    rw [sub_sub_cancel] at h3
    exact h3
  exact (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal L).ne_top ((Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).mpr h2)

/-- **Cohen–Macaulayness of a local ring is invariant under a ring isomorphism.** Both the depth
along the maximal ideal and the Krull dimension are. -/
public theorem isMaximalCohenMacaulay_of_ringEquiv {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [IsLocalRing A] [IsLocalRing B] (e : A ≃+* B)
    (h : Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay A A) : Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay B B := by
  rw [Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay, ← IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective
      (e : A →+* B) e.surjective, ← Module.depth_eq_of_ringEquiv e,
    ← ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv e]
  exact h

/-- **Lemma 00P2, in the form used here: the local dimension and the height trade off along a
surjection.** Let `k` be a field, let `f : S' → S` be a surjection of `k`-algebras with `S'` of
finite type, let `x` be a point of `Spec S` and let `y` be the point `f⁻¹(x)` of `Spec S'`. Then
$$
  \dim_y \operatorname{Spec} S' + \operatorname{height} x
    = \dim_x \operatorname{Spec} S + \operatorname{height} y,
$$
so that the two local dimensions differ by exactly the amount by which the two heights differ.

This is Lemma 00P1 read at both points: it computes `dim_y Spec S' = height y + trdeg_k κ(y)` and
`dim_x Spec S = height x + trdeg_k κ(x)`, and the two residue fields agree — `f` is surjective,
hence surjective on stalks, so `κ(y) → κ(x)` is bijective and `AlgEquiv.lift_trdeg_eq` equates
the transcendence degrees, which may a priori be cardinals in different universes. Cancelling the
common transcendence degree is what the additive form does without subtracting in `WithBot ℕ∞`.

The point `y` is taken as a hypothesis `y.asIdeal = x.asIdeal.comap f` rather than as
`PrimeSpectrum.comap f x`, so that the point at which the lemma is used may be named on its own
terms; the two forms are `rfl`-interchangeable. -/
public theorem localKrullDim_add_height_comm (k : Type*) [Field k] {S' : Type*} {S : Type*}
    [CommRing S'] [CommRing S] [Algebra k S'] [Algebra k S] [Algebra.FiniteType k S']
    (f : S' →ₐ[k] S) (hf : Function.Surjective f) (x : PrimeSpectrum S) (y : PrimeSpectrum S')
    (hy : y.asIdeal = x.asIdeal.comap f.toRingHom) :
    TopologicalSpace.localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S') y + (x.asIdeal.height : WithBot ℕ∞)
      = TopologicalSpace.localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S) x
        + (y.asIdeal.height : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have hft : Algebra.FiniteType k S := .of_surjective f hf
  have e : y.asIdeal.ResidueField ≃ₐ[k] x.asIdeal.ResidueField :=
    AlgEquiv.ofBijective (Ideal.ResidueField.mapₐ y.asIdeal x.asIdeal f hy)
      ((RingHom.surjectiveOnStalks_of_surjective hf).residueFieldMap_bijective
        y.asIdeal x.asIdeal hy)
  have key : Cardinal.toENat (Algebra.trdeg k y.asIdeal.ResidueField)
      = Cardinal.toENat (Algebra.trdeg k x.asIdeal.ResidueField) := by
    simpa using congrArg Cardinal.toENat e.lift_trdeg_eq
  rw [PrimeSpectrum.localKrullDim_eq_height_add_trdeg_residueField k y,
    PrimeSpectrum.localKrullDim_eq_height_add_trdeg_residueField k x, key]
  push_cast
  abel

end General

/-- The sublevel set `{𝔮 | dim_𝔮(T/R) + i ≤ d}` of the relative dimension of a finite type ring
map `R → T` is open in `Spec T`. For `i ≤ d` it is the sublevel set of Lemma 00QH at the bound
`d - i`, and for `i > d` it is empty, relative dimension being never `-∞`. -/
public theorem isOpen_setOf_relativeDimensionAt_add_le (R : Type*) {T : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing T] [Algebra R T] [Algebra.FiniteType R T] (d i : ℕ) :
    IsOpen {Q : PrimeSpectrum T |
      Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal + (i : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞)} := by
  by_cases hid : i ≤ d
  · have : {Q : PrimeSpectrum T |
        Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal + (i : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞)} =
        {Q : PrimeSpectrum T |
          Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal ≤ ((d - i : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞)} := by
      ext Q
      exact add_natCast_le_natCast_iff (Algebra.zero_le_relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal) hid
    rw [this]
    exact Algebra.isOpen_setOf_relativeDimensionAt_le (d - i)
  · have : {Q : PrimeSpectrum T |
        Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal + (i : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞)} = ∅ := by
      ext Q
      refine iff_of_false (fun h ↦ hid ?_) (Set.notMem_empty Q)
      exact_mod_cast le_trans (le_add_of_nonneg_left
        (Algebra.zero_le_relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal)) h
    rw [this]
    exact isOpen_empty

section Content

variable {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [Algebra.FiniteType R S] {d : ℕ}

/-- The hypothesis of Stacks 00RA on the fibres of `R → S`: every nonempty fibre is
Cohen–Macaulay and equidimensional of dimension `d`. -/
public def FibresCM (R S : Type*) [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (d : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime], Nontrivial (p.Fiber S) →
    (∀ (Q : Ideal (p.Fiber S)) [Q.IsPrime],
        Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay (Localization.AtPrime Q) (Localization.AtPrime Q)) ∧
      TopologicalSpace.Equidimensional (PrimeSpectrum (p.Fiber S)) ∧
      ringKrullDim (p.Fiber S) = (d : WithBot ℕ∞)

/-! ### The fibre through a prime, and Lemma 00P1 on it -/

/-- The point of the fibre `Spec (κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S)` corresponding to a prime `𝔮` of `S`, where
`𝔭 = R ∩ 𝔮`: the image of `𝔮` under `PrimeSpectrum.preimageEquivFiber`. -/
public noncomputable def fiberPoint (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] : PrimeSpectrum ((q.under R).Fiber S) :=
  PrimeSpectrum.preimageEquivFiber R S ⟨q.under R, inferInstance⟩ ⟨⟨q, ‹_›⟩, rfl⟩

/-- The relative dimension `dim_𝔮(S/R)` of Definition 00QD is the local dimension of the fibre
`Spec (κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S)` at the point `q̄` corresponding to `𝔮`, where `𝔭 = R ∩ 𝔮`: the fibre subspace
of `Spec S` through `𝔮`, on which the definition takes it, is homeomorphic to
`Spec (κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S)` by `PrimeSpectrum.preimageHomeomorphFiber`, carrying `𝔮` to `q̄`.

Read together with Lemma 00P1, applied to the fibre — a finite type algebra over the field
`κ(𝔭)` — this says `dim_𝔮(S/R) = dim(S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮) + trdeg_{κ(𝔭)} κ(𝔮)`. -/
public theorem relativeDimensionAt_eq_localKrullDim_fiber (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] :
    Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R q = TopologicalSpace.localKrullDim
      (PrimeSpectrum ((q.under R).Fiber S)) (fiberPoint R q) := by
  rw [Algebra.relativeDimensionAt,
    ← TopologicalSpace.topologicalKrullDimAt_eq_localKrullDim]
  exact topologicalKrullDimAt_eq_of_homeomorph (PrimeSpectrum.preimageHomeomorphFiber R S _) _

/-- The relative dimension at `𝔮` is at most the dimension of the whole fibre through `𝔮`: the
dimension of a space at a point is at most the dimension of the space, taken here on
`Spec (κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S)`. -/
public theorem relativeDimensionAt_le_ringKrullDim_fiber (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] :
    Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R q ≤ ringKrullDim ((q.under R).Fiber S) := by
  rw [Algebra.relativeDimensionAt,
    topologicalKrullDimAt_eq_of_homeomorph (PrimeSpectrum.preimageHomeomorphFiber R S _),
    topologicalKrullDimAt, ← PrimeSpectrum.topologicalKrullDim_eq_ringKrullDim]
  exact iInf_le_of_le ⟨Set.univ, Set.mem_univ _, isOpen_univ⟩
    (IsHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq _ (Homeomorph.Set.univ _).isHomeomorph).le

/-! ### The local ring `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` of the fibre -/

/-- The local ring of the fibre at a prime is unchanged when the prime is rewritten: an equality
of primes of `S` gives an equality of the ideals that the localization is divided by. -/
public def fiberLocalRingEquivOfEq (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] {r q : Ideal S} [r.IsPrime] [q.IsPrime] (h : r = q) :
    (Localization.AtPrime r ⧸
        ((q.under R).map (algebraMap R S)).map (algebraMap S (Localization.AtPrime r))) ≃+*
      fiberLocalRing R q := by
  subst h
  exact Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (by rw [Ideal.map_map, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq])

/-- The point `q̄` of the fibre `Spec (κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S)` attached to a prime `𝔮` of `S` contracts to
`𝔮` along `S → κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S`: the inverse of the equivalence `PrimeSpectrum.preimageEquivFiber`
which attaches it is contraction along `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight`. -/
public theorem comap_includeRight_fiberPoint (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (q : Ideal S) [hq : q.IsPrime] :
    (fiberPoint R q).asIdeal.comap
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight (R := R) (A := (q.under R).ResidueField)
          (B := S)).toRingHom = q := by
  have h3 : (PrimeSpectrum.preimageHomeomorphFiber R S
        (⟨q.under R, inferInstance⟩ : PrimeSpectrum R)).symm (fiberPoint R q) = ⟨⟨q, hq⟩, rfl⟩ :=
    (PrimeSpectrum.preimageHomeomorphFiber R S _).symm_apply_apply _
  have h2 := PrimeSpectrum.coe_preimageHomeomorphFiber_symm_apply_coe_asIdeal R S
    (⟨q.under R, inferInstance⟩ : PrimeSpectrum R) (fiberPoint R q)
  rw [h3] at h2
  exact SetLike.coe_injective h2.symm

/-- **The local ring of the fibre through `𝔮` is `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮`.** The localization of the fibre
`κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S` at the point `q̄` corresponding to `𝔮` is `Ideal.Fiber.algEquivAux₂`, whose target is
`S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` once the contraction of `q̄` to `S` is identified with `𝔮` and the ideal `(𝔭S)S_𝔮`
with `𝔭S_𝔮` (`Ideal.map_map`). -/
public noncomputable def localizationFiberPointEquiv (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] :
    Localization.AtPrime (fiberPoint R q).asIdeal ≃+* fiberLocalRing R q :=
  (Ideal.Fiber.algEquivAux₂ (R := R) (S := S) (p := q.under R)
      (fiberPoint R q).asIdeal).toRingEquiv.trans
    (fiberLocalRingEquivOfEq R (by exact comap_includeRight_fiberPoint R q))

/-- `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` is Noetherian: it is the localization at a prime of the fibre `κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S`, a
finite type algebra over a field. -/
public theorem isNoetherianRing_fiberLocalRing (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] [Algebra.FiniteType R S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] :
    IsNoetherianRing (fiberLocalRing R q) := by
  have : IsNoetherianRing ((q.under R).Fiber S) :=
    Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing (q.under R).ResidueField ((q.under R).Fiber S)
  exact isNoetherianRing_of_ringEquiv _ (localizationFiberPointEquiv R q)

/-- `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` is a local ring: it is the localization at a prime of the fibre `κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S`. -/
public theorem isLocalRing_fiberLocalRing (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] : IsLocalRing (fiberLocalRing R q) :=
  RingEquiv.isLocalRing (localizationFiberPointEquiv R q)

/-- The fibre of `Spec S → Spec R` through `𝔮` is nonempty, so `κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S` is not the zero
ring: it has the point `q̄`. -/
public theorem nontrivial_fiber (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] : Nontrivial ((q.under R).Fiber S) := by
  refine not_subsingleton_iff_nontrivial.mp fun h ↦ (fiberPoint R q).isPrime.ne_top ?_
  exact (Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).mpr
    (Subsingleton.elim (1 : (q.under R).Fiber S) 0 ▸ (fiberPoint R q).asIdeal.zero_mem)

/-- **The local ring `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` of the fibre through `𝔮` is Cohen–Macaulay** as soon as all the
local rings of the fibre `κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S` are, `𝔭 = R ∩ 𝔮`: it is the localization of that fibre at
the point corresponding to `𝔮` (`localizationFiberPointEquiv`), and Cohen–Macaulayness of a local
ring is invariant under a ring isomorphism. -/
public theorem _root_.Algebra.isMaximalCohenMacaulay_quotient_map_under_localizationAtPrime
    {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime]
    [IsLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸
      (q.under R).map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q)))]
    (hCM : ∀ (Q : Ideal ((q.under R).Fiber S)) [Q.IsPrime],
      Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay (Localization.AtPrime Q) (Localization.AtPrime Q)) :
    Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay
      (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸ (q.under R).map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q)))
      (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸ (q.under R).map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q))) :=
  isMaximalCohenMacaulay_of_ringEquiv (localizationFiberPointEquiv R q)
    (hCM (fiberPoint R q).asIdeal)

/-! ### Passing to `S̄ = S/(f₁, …, f_i)` -/

/-- The local ring of the fibre of `Spec (S/I) → Spec R` at a prime `Q` is the local ring of the
fibre of `Spec S → Spec R` at the prime `𝔮 = Q ∩ S` divided by `I`: passing to the fibre and
localizing both commute with the quotient, so both rings are `S_𝔮/(𝔭S_𝔮 + IS_𝔮)`.

The localization of `S/I` at `Q` is `S_𝔮/IS_𝔮` because the image of `S ∖ 𝔮` in `S/I` is exactly
`(S/I) ∖ Q` (`Ideal.algebraMapSubmonoid_primeCompl_of_liesOver_surjective`); dividing further by
`𝔭` and rearranging the two quotients (`DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotSup`) gives the claim. -/
public theorem ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_quotient (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (I : Ideal S) (Q : Ideal (S ⧸ I)) [Q.IsPrime] (q : Ideal S)
    [q.IsPrime] (hq : q = Q.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) :
    ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R Q)
      = ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R q ⧸ I.map (algebraMap S (fiberLocalRing R q))) := by
  subst hq
  set q : Ideal S := Q.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) with hqdef
  have : Q.LiesOver q := ⟨rfl⟩
  set Sq := Localization.AtPrime q with hSq
  set I' : Ideal Sq := I.map (algebraMap S Sq) with hI'
  set P' : Ideal Sq := (q.under R).map (algebraMap R Sq) with hP'
  have hsub : Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (S ⧸ I) q.primeCompl = Q.primeCompl :=
    Ideal.algebraMapSubmonoid_primeCompl_of_liesOver_surjective (P := Q) q
      Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have : IsLocalization.AtPrime (Sq ⧸ I') Q := by
    rw [IsLocalization.AtPrime, ← hsub]; infer_instance
  have : IsScalarTower R (S ⧸ I) (Sq ⧸ I') := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq (fun _ => rfl)
  have e₁ : Localization.AtPrime Q ≃ₐ[S ⧸ I] (Sq ⧸ I') :=
    IsLocalization.algEquiv Q.primeCompl _ _
  have hQR : Q.under R = q.under R := rfl
  have step1 : ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R Q)
      = ringKrullDim ((Sq ⧸ I') ⧸ (q.under R).map (algebraMap R (Sq ⧸ I'))) := by
    refine ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (Ideal.quotientEquiv _ _ (e₁.restrictScalars R) ?_)
    rw [hQR, Ideal.map_map]
    congr 1
    exact (AlgHom.comp_algebraMap (e₁.restrictScalars R).toAlgHom).symm
  have step2 : ringKrullDim ((Sq ⧸ I') ⧸ (q.under R).map (algebraMap R (Sq ⧸ I')))
      = ringKrullDim (Sq ⧸ (I' ⊔ P')) := by
    have hid : (q.under R).map (algebraMap R (Sq ⧸ I')) = P'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I') := by
      rw [hP', Ideal.map_map]; rfl
    rw [hid]
    exact ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotSup I' P')
  have step3 : ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R q ⧸ I.map (algebraMap S (fiberLocalRing R q)))
      = ringKrullDim (Sq ⧸ (P' ⊔ I')) := by
    have hid : I.map (algebraMap S (fiberLocalRing R q)) = I'.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk P') := by
      rw [hI', Ideal.map_map]; rfl
    rw [hid]
    exact ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotSup P' I')
  rw [step1, step2, step3, sup_comm]

/-! ### The fibre of the quotient -/

/-- The point of the fibre attached to a prime `𝔮` of `S` is the *only* point of the fibre that
contracts to `𝔮` along `S → κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S`, the inverse of `PrimeSpectrum.preimageEquivFiber` being
that contraction. -/
public theorem eq_fiberPoint (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] (x : PrimeSpectrum ((q.under R).Fiber S))
    (hx : x.asIdeal.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight (R := R)
        (A := (q.under R).ResidueField) (B := S)).toRingHom = q) :
    x = fiberPoint R q := by
  set p : PrimeSpectrum R := ⟨q.under R, inferInstance⟩
  have h1 := PrimeSpectrum.coe_preimageHomeomorphFiber_symm_apply_coe_asIdeal R S p x
  have h2 := PrimeSpectrum.coe_preimageHomeomorphFiber_symm_apply_coe_asIdeal R S p
    (fiberPoint R q)
  have key : (PrimeSpectrum.preimageHomeomorphFiber R S p).symm x
      = (PrimeSpectrum.preimageHomeomorphFiber R S p).symm (fiberPoint R q) := by
    refine Subtype.ext (PrimeSpectrum.ext (SetLike.coe_injective ?_))
    rw [h1, h2]
    exact congrArg (fun J : Ideal S => (J : Set S))
      (hx.trans (comap_includeRight_fiberPoint R q).symm)
  simpa using congrArg (PrimeSpectrum.preimageHomeomorphFiber R S p) key

/-- **The fibres of `Spec (S/I) → Spec R` sit inside those of `Spec S → Spec R`.** The surjection
`S → S/I` induces a surjection `κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S → κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S/I` of fibres over `𝔭`. -/
public noncomputable def fiberMapQuotient (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] (I : Ideal S) :
    p.Fiber S →ₐ[p.ResidueField] p.Fiber (S ⧸ I) :=
  Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id p.ResidueField p.ResidueField) (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ R I)

public theorem fiberMapQuotient_surjective (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] (I : Ideal S) :
    Function.Surjective (fiberMapQuotient R p I) :=
  Algebra.TensorProduct.map_surjective _ _ (fun x => ⟨x, rfl⟩) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

public theorem fiberMapQuotient_includeRight (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R S] (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] (I : Ideal S) (x : S) :
    fiberMapQuotient R p I (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight
        (R := R) (A := p.ResidueField) (B := S) x)
      = Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight (R := R) (A := p.ResidueField) (B := S ⧸ I)
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk I x) := by
  simp [fiberMapQuotient]

/-- The dimension of the local ring `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` of the fibre through `𝔮` is the height of the
point `q̄` of the fibre `Spec (κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S)` corresponding to `𝔮`: that local ring is a
localization of the fibre at `q̄` (`localizationFiberPointEquiv`). -/
public theorem ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_eq_height (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] :
    ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R q) = ((fiberPoint R q).asIdeal.height : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
  (ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (localizationFiberPointEquiv R q)).symm.trans
    (IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height (fiberPoint R q).asIdeal
      (Localization.AtPrime (fiberPoint R q).asIdeal))

/-- `dim(S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮)` is not `⊥`: the ring is local, hence nonzero. -/
public theorem ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_ne_bot (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] :
    ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R q) ≠ ⊥ := by
  have := isLocalRing_fiberLocalRing R q
  intro h
  have h0 : (0 : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R q) :=
    ringKrullDim_nonneg_of_nontrivial
  rw [h] at h0
  simp at h0

/-- `dim(S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮)` is not `⊤`: the ring is Noetherian local. -/
public theorem ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_ne_top (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [Algebra.FiniteType R S] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] :
    ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R q) ≠ ⊤ := by
  have := isNoetherianRing_fiberLocalRing R q
  have := isLocalRing_fiberLocalRing R q
  exact ringKrullDim_ne_top

/-- **The point of the fibre of `S̄ = S/I` above `Q` lies over the point of the fibre of `S` above
`𝔮 = I ∩ Q`.** Contracting `Q̄` along the surjection `κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S → κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S̄` of fibres gives
`q̄`: both contract to `𝔮` along `S → κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S`, and `q̄` is the only point of the fibre that
does (`eq_fiberPoint`). -/
public theorem comap_fiberMapQuotient_fiberPoint (R : Type*) {S : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (I : Ideal S) (Q : Ideal (S ⧸ I)) [Q.IsPrime] :
    PrimeSpectrum.comap (fiberMapQuotient R (Q.under R) I).toRingHom (fiberPoint R Q)
      = fiberPoint R (Q.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) := by
  refine eq_fiberPoint R (Q.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) _ ?_
  have hcomp : (fiberMapQuotient R (Q.under R) I).toRingHom.comp
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight (R := R) (A := (Q.under R).ResidueField)
          (B := S)).toRingHom
      = (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight (R := R) (A := (Q.under R).ResidueField)
          (B := S ⧸ I)).toRingHom.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) :=
    RingHom.ext fun x => fiberMapQuotient_includeRight R (Q.under R) I x
  change ((fiberPoint R Q).asIdeal.comap (fiberMapQuotient R (Q.under R) I).toRingHom).comap
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight (R := R) (A := (Q.under R).ResidueField)
        (B := S)).toRingHom = Q.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)
  rw [Ideal.comap_comap, hcomp, ← Ideal.comap_comap, comap_includeRight_fiberPoint R Q]

/-- **Step 1 of the proof (Lemma 00P1, in the form of Lemma 00P2).** For a prime `Q` of
`S̄ = S/I` contracting to `𝔮` in `S`, the relative dimensions over `R` at `𝔮` and at `Q` differ by
the same amount as the dimensions of the local rings `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` and `S̄_Q/𝔭S̄_Q` of their fibres:
$$
  \dim_𝔮(S/R) + \dim(S̄_Q/𝔭S̄_Q) = \dim_Q(S̄/R) + \dim(S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮).
$$
This is the source's `dim_𝔮(S/R) = dim(S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮) + trdeg_{κ(𝔭)} κ(𝔮)` (Lemma 00P1) applied at
both points, the two transcendence degrees being equal; in that additive form it is exactly
Lemma 00P2 (`localKrullDim_add_height_comm`, deduced from Lemma 00P1 above) for the surjection
`κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S → κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S̄` of fibres, whose `Spec` carries `Q̄` to
`q̄` (`comap_fiberMapQuotient_fiberPoint`), since a relative dimension is the local dimension of a
fibre (`relativeDimensionAt_eq_localKrullDim_fiber`) and the dimension of the local ring of the
fibre is the height of the point (`ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_eq_height`). Writing it this way
keeps the transcendence degree out of the statement. -/
public theorem relativeDimensionAt_add_ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_comm (R : Type*) {S : Type*}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [Algebra.FiniteType R S] (I : Ideal S)
    (Q : Ideal (S ⧸ I)) [Q.IsPrime] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime]
    (hq : q = Q.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)) :
    Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R q + ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R Q)
      = Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q + ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R q) := by
  subst hq
  have h := localKrullDim_add_height_comm ((Q.under R).ResidueField)
    (fiberMapQuotient R (Q.under R) I) (fiberMapQuotient_surjective R (Q.under R) I)
    (fiberPoint R Q) (fiberPoint R (Q.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)))
    (congrArg PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal (comap_fiberMapQuotient_fiberPoint R I Q).symm)
  rw [relativeDimensionAt_eq_localKrullDim_fiber R (Q.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)),
    relativeDimensionAt_eq_localKrullDim_fiber R Q,
    ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_eq_height R (Q.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)),
    ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_eq_height R Q]
  exact h

/-- The local ring of the fibre of `S̄ = S/(f₁, …, f_i)` at `Q` has the dimension of
`A/(f₁, …, f_i)`, where `A = S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` is the local ring of the fibre of `S` at `𝔮 = Q ∩ S`. -/
private theorem ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_eq_quotient_ofList (R : Type*) {S : Type*}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (f : List S) (Q : Ideal (S ⧸ Ideal.ofList f))
    [Q.IsPrime] (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime] (hq : q = Q.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.ofList f))) :
    ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R Q) = ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R q ⧸
      Ideal.ofList (f.map (algebraMap S (fiberLocalRing R q)))) := by
  rw [ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_quotient R (Ideal.ofList f) Q q hq, Ideal.map_ofList]

/-- **Step 1 of the proof (Lemmas 00P1 and 00KW).** If `f₁, …, f_i` is a regular sequence in the
local ring `A = S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` of the fibre through `𝔮`, then the relative dimension of
`S̄ = S/(f₁, …, f_i)` at `𝔮` satisfies `dim_𝔮(S̄/R) + i ≤ d`.

Indeed `dim_𝔮(S/R) = dim A + t` and `dim_𝔮(S̄/R) = dim Ā + t` for one and the same transcendence
degree `t` (`exists_relativeDimensionAt_eq_ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_add`), while `Ā` is
`A/(f₁, …, f_i)` (`ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_quotient`), so `dim Ā + i = dim A` by Lemma 00KW,
Mathlib's `ringKrullDim_add_length_eq_ringKrullDim_of_isRegular`, in the Noetherian local ring
`A`. Adding `t` to that equality gives `dim_𝔮(S̄/R) + i = dim_𝔮(S/R)`, which is at most `d`
because the fibre through `𝔮` has dimension `d`. -/
public theorem relativeDimensionAt_add_length_le_of_isRegular (hfib : FibresCM R S d)
    (f : List S) (Q : PrimeSpectrum (S ⧸ Ideal.ofList f)) (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime]
    (hq : q = Q.asIdeal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.ofList f)))
    (hreg : IsRegular (fiberLocalRing R q) (f.map (algebraMap S (fiberLocalRing R q)))) :
    Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal + (f.length : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have := isNoetherianRing_fiberLocalRing R q
  have := isLocalRing_fiberLocalRing R q
  have hstar := relativeDimensionAt_add_ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_comm R (Ideal.ofList f)
    Q.asIdeal q hq
  have hKW := ringKrullDim_add_length_eq_ringKrullDim_of_isRegular
    (f.map (algebraMap S (fiberLocalRing R q))) hreg
  rw [List.length_map] at hKW
  have hA := ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_eq_quotient_ofList R f Q.asIdeal q hq
  have hle : Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R q ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    (relativeDimensionAt_le_ringKrullDim_fiber R q).trans_eq
      (hfib (q.under R) (nontrivial_fiber R q)).2.2
  refine le_trans (le_of_eq (add_right_cancel_of_ne_bot_of_ne_top
    (ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_ne_bot R Q.asIdeal)
    (ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_ne_top R Q.asIdeal) ?_)) hle
  rw [hstar, ← hKW, ← hA, ← add_assoc]
  exact add_right_comm _ _ _


public theorem isRegular_of_relativeDimensionAt_add_length_le_of_eq (hfib : FibresCM R S d)
    (f : List S) (Q : PrimeSpectrum (S ⧸ Ideal.ofList f)) (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime]
    (hq : q = Q.asIdeal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.ofList f)))
    (hQ : Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal + (f.length : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    IsRegular (fiberLocalRing R q) (f.map (algebraMap S (fiberLocalRing R q))) := by
  have hnoeth := isNoetherianRing_fiberLocalRing R q
  have hlocA := isLocalRing_fiberLocalRing R q
  have hnt := nontrivial_fiber R q
  have hfq : Ideal.ofList f ≤ q := by
    rw [hq, ← Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap, Ideal.map_quotient_self]
    exact bot_le
  have hmem : ∀ x ∈ f.map (algebraMap S (fiberLocalRing R q)),
      x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (fiberLocalRing R q) := by
    intro z hz
    obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := List.mem_map.mp hz
    have hJ : (q.under R).map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q))
        ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) := by
      rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
      intro r hr
      have h1 : algebraMap R S r ∈ q := hr
      have h2 := (IsLocalization.AtPrime.to_map_mem_maximal_iff (Localization.AtPrime q) q
        (algebraMap R S r)).mpr h1
      simpa [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R S (Localization.AtPrime q)] using h2
    have hy : algebraMap S (Localization.AtPrime q) x
        ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) :=
      (IsLocalization.AtPrime.to_map_mem_maximal_iff (Localization.AtPrime q) q x).mpr
        (hfq (Ideal.subset_span hx))
    exact mk_mem_maximalIdeal_quotient hJ hy
  have hCM : Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay (fiberLocalRing R q) (fiberLocalRing R q) :=
    isMaximalCohenMacaulay_of_ringEquiv (localizationFiberPointEquiv R q)
      ((hfib (q.under R) hnt).1 (fiberPoint R q).asIdeal)
  have hdq : Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R q = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    rw [relativeDimensionAt_eq_localKrullDim_fiber R q,
      Stacks.CohenMacaulay.EquidimensionalCut.localKrullDim_eq_ringKrullDim (q.under R).ResidueField
        (hfib (q.under R) hnt).2.1
        (fiberPoint R q), (hfib (q.under R) hnt).2.2]
  have hstar := relativeDimensionAt_add_ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_comm R (Ideal.ofList f)
    Q.asIdeal q hq
  have hAQ := ringKrullDim_fiberLocalRing_eq_quotient_ofList R f Q.asIdeal q hq
  have hge : ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (fiberLocalRing R q)).height : WithBot ℕ∞)
      ≤ ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R q ⧸
          Ideal.ofList (f.map (algebraMap S (fiberLocalRing R q))))
        + ((f.map (algebraMap S (fiberLocalRing R q))).length : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    Stacks.CohenMacaulay.EquidimensionalCut.height_le_ringKrullDim_quotient_ofList_add_length
      (Submodule.span_le.mpr hmem)
  have hdQle : Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    le_trans (le_add_of_nonneg_right (by exact_mod_cast Nat.zero_le f.length)) hQ
  refine (Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay.isRegular_iff_ringKrullDim_add_length_eq_ringKrullDim
    hCM _ hmem).1.mpr (le_antisymm ?_ ?_)
  · rw [List.length_map, ← hAQ]
    refine le_of_add_le_add_right_of_ne_bot_of_ne_top
      (c := Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal) ?_ ?_ ?_
    · intro hbot
      have h0 := Algebra.zero_le_relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal
      rw [hbot] at h0
      simp at h0
    · intro htop
      rw [htop] at hdQle
      exact absurd (top_le_iff.mp hdQle) (natCast_ne_top_withBot d)
    · calc ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R Q.asIdeal) + (f.length : WithBot ℕ∞)
            + Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal
          = ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R Q.asIdeal)
              + (Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal + (f.length : WithBot ℕ∞)) := by
            rw [add_assoc, add_comm ((f.length : WithBot ℕ∞))]
        _ ≤ ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R Q.asIdeal) + (d : WithBot ℕ∞) := add_le_add le_rfl hQ
        _ = Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R q + ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R Q.asIdeal) := by
            rw [hdq]; exact add_comm _ _
        _ = Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal + ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R q) := hstar
        _ = ringKrullDim (fiberLocalRing R q) + Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal :=
            add_comm _ _
  · rw [← IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_height_eq_ringKrullDim]
    exact hge

/-- **Step 2 of the proof (Lemma 00R9).** If the relative dimension of `S̄ = S/(f₁, …, f_i)` at `𝔮`
satisfies `dim_𝔮(S̄/R) + i ≤ d`, then `f₁, …, f_i` is a regular sequence in the local ring
`A = S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` of the fibre through `𝔮`.

The fibre through `𝔮` is Cohen–Macaulay and equidimensional of dimension `d`, so its local
dimension at `q̄` is `d` (`Stacks.CohenMacaulay.EquidimensionalCut.localKrullDim_eq_ringKrullDim`),
which by Lemma 00P1 reads
`dim A + t = d` with `t` the transcendence degree of `κ(q̄)` over `κ(𝔭)`. The hypothesis reads
`dim Ā + t + i ≤ d` for the same `t`, so `dim Ā + i ≤ dim A`, and Krull's height theorem gives
the reverse inequality; `f₁, …, f_i` therefore cuts the dimension of the Cohen–Macaulay local
ring `A` down by exactly `i`, which by Lemma 02JN — the local form of Lemma 00R9 — makes it a
regular sequence in `A`. -/
public theorem isRegular_of_relativeDimensionAt_add_length_le (hfib : FibresCM R S d)
    (f : List S) (Q : PrimeSpectrum (S ⧸ Ideal.ofList f))
    (hQ : Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal + (f.length : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    IsRegular (fiberLocalRing R (Q.asIdeal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.ofList f))))
      (f.map (algebraMap S
        (fiberLocalRing R (Q.asIdeal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.ofList f)))))) :=
  isRegular_of_relativeDimensionAt_add_length_le_of_eq hfib f Q _ rfl hQ


/-- The set of Stacks 00RA, read on `Spec S̄`, is the sublevel set `{Q | dim_Q(S̄/R) + i ≤ d}` of
the relative dimension of `S̄ = S/(f₁, …, f_i)`. -/
public theorem isRegular_iff_relativeDimensionAt_add_length_le (hfib : FibresCM R S d)
    (f : List S) (Q : PrimeSpectrum (S ⧸ Ideal.ofList f)) :
    IsRegular (fiberLocalRing R (Q.asIdeal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.ofList f))))
      (f.map (algebraMap S
        (fiberLocalRing R (Q.asIdeal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.ofList f)))))) ↔
      Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal + (f.length : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
  ⟨relativeDimensionAt_add_length_le_of_isRegular hfib f Q _ rfl,
    isRegular_of_relativeDimensionAt_add_length_le hfib f Q⟩

end Content

/-- **Stacks 00RA.** Let `R → S` be a finite type ring map and let `d` be such that every
nonempty fibre `S ⊗_R κ(𝔭)` is Cohen–Macaulay and equidimensional of dimension `d`. Let
`f = f₁, …, f_i` be elements of `S`. Then the set of points `𝔮` of `V(f₁, …, f_i)` at which
`f₁, …, f_i` is a regular sequence in `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮`, where `𝔭 = R ∩ 𝔮`, is open in
`V(f₁, …, f_i)`. -/
public theorem solution
    {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [Algebra.FiniteType R S] (d : ℕ)
    (hfib : ∀ (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime], Nontrivial (p.Fiber S) →
      (∀ (Q : Ideal (p.Fiber S)) [Q.IsPrime],
          Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay (Localization.AtPrime Q) (Localization.AtPrime Q)) ∧
        TopologicalSpace.Equidimensional (PrimeSpectrum (p.Fiber S)) ∧
        ringKrullDim (p.Fiber S) = (d : WithBot ℕ∞))
    (f : List S) :
    IsOpen {q : ↥(PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Ideal.ofList f : Set S)) |
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular
        (Localization.AtPrime q.1.asIdeal ⧸
          (q.1.asIdeal.under R).map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q.1.asIdeal)))
        (f.map (algebraMap S (Localization.AtPrime q.1.asIdeal ⧸
          (q.1.asIdeal.under R).map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q.1.asIdeal)))))} := by
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.ofList f)) :=
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have hemb : Topology.IsClosedEmbedding
      (PrimeSpectrum.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.ofList f))) :=
    PrimeSpectrum.isClosedEmbedding_comap_of_surjective _ _ hsurj
  have hrange : Set.range (PrimeSpectrum.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.ofList f))) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Ideal.ofList f : Set S) := by
    rw [range_comap_of_surjective _ _ hsurj, Ideal.mk_ker]
  let e : PrimeSpectrum (S ⧸ Ideal.ofList f) ≃ₜ
      ↥(PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Ideal.ofList f : Set S)) :=
    hemb.isEmbedding.toHomeomorph.trans (Homeomorph.setCongr hrange)
  rw [← e.isOpen_preimage]
  have hset : (e ⁻¹' {q : ↥(PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Ideal.ofList f : Set S)) |
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular
        (Localization.AtPrime q.1.asIdeal ⧸
          (q.1.asIdeal.under R).map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q.1.asIdeal)))
        (f.map (algebraMap S (Localization.AtPrime q.1.asIdeal ⧸
          (q.1.asIdeal.under R).map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q.1.asIdeal)))))}) =
      {Q : PrimeSpectrum (S ⧸ Ideal.ofList f) |
        Algebra.relativeDimensionAt R Q.asIdeal + (f.length : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤
          (d : WithBot ℕ∞)} := by
    ext Q
    exact isRegular_iff_relativeDimensionAt_add_length_le hfib f Q
  rw [hset]
  exact isOpen_setOf_relativeDimensionAt_add_le R d f.length

end Stacks.RegularSequence.FibrewiseLocus

/-!
# Openness of the locus where a sequence is regular in the fibres

Let `R → S` be a ring map of finite type all of whose fibres `S ⊗_R κ(𝔭)` are Cohen–Macaulay and
equidimensional of one and the same dimension `d`, and let `f₁, …, f_i` be elements of `S`. At a
point `𝔮` of `V(f₁, …, f_i)`, lying over `𝔭 = R ∩ 𝔮`, one may ask whether `f₁, …, f_i` is a
regular sequence *relative to `R`* at `𝔮`, that is a regular sequence in the local ring
`S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` of the fibre through `𝔮` at `𝔮`. This file states that this is an open condition on
`V(f₁, …, f_i)`.

The reason is a dimension count, and it is local on the fibre: by Lemma 00P1 the relative
dimension `dim_𝔮(S/R)` splits as `dim(S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮) + trdeg_{κ(𝔭)} κ(𝔮)`, so at a point of the set
the passage to `S̄ = S/(f₁, …, f_i)` drops the relative dimension by exactly `i` (Lemma 00KW),
and the relative dimension of `S̄/R` is upper semicontinuous (Lemma 00QH). On a neighbourhood
of such a point the fibres of `S̄` therefore have dimension at most `d - i`, which by Lemma 00R9,
applied to the Cohen–Macaulay equidimensional fibre, is enough to make `f₁, …, f_i` a regular
sequence at every point of that neighbourhood.

## Main results

* `Algebra.isOpen_setOf_isRegular_fiber_of_isMaximalCohenMacaulay_of_equidimensional`: the set of
  points of `V(f₁, …, f_i)` at which `f₁, …, f_i` is a regular sequence in `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` is open in
  `V(f₁, …, f_i)`.

## Implementation notes

`V(f₁, …, f_i)` is the closed subspace `PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus ↑(Ideal.ofList f)` of
`PrimeSpectrum S`, and "open in `V(f₁, …, f_i)`" is `IsOpen` for the subspace topology on it, so
that the source's set is a set of points of `V(f₁, …, f_i)` rather than a set of points of
`Spec S` intersected with it. The source's `f₁, …, f_i` is a `List S`, so `i` is `f.length` and
`(f₁, …, f_i)` is `Ideal.ofList f = Ideal.span {x | x ∈ f}`; this is the shape Mathlib's regular
sequence API (`RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular`) is phrased in, and it covers `i = 0`, where the
statement reads that `Spec S` is open in itself.

The local ring `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` of the fibre is spelled as the source spells it, as the quotient
`Localization.AtPrime 𝔮 ⧸ 𝔭.map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime 𝔮))` of the localization by
the ideal generated by the image of `𝔭`, extended along `R → S_𝔮` in one step. It agrees with
`𝔭.Fiber (Localization.AtPrime 𝔮) = κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S_𝔮`, the spelling of tag 00PK, by
`Ideal.Fiber.ringEquivQuotient`, and with the local ring of the fibre `κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S` at the point
of it corresponding to `𝔮` by `Ideal.Fiber.algEquivAux₂`. The quotient is chosen over the tensor
product because it carries the canonical `S`-algebra structure through which the source's own
elements are mapped: `algebraMap S (S_𝔮 ⧸ 𝔭S_𝔮)` is `Ideal.Quotient.mk _ ∘ algebraMap S S_𝔮` by
`rfl`, whereas `κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S_𝔮` is an `S`-algebra only through
`Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra`, which is not an instance.

The prime `𝔭` is not an argument: it is `𝔮.under R`, Mathlib's `Ideal.comap (algebraMap R S) 𝔮`,
which is the source's `R ∩ 𝔮`. The localization is the concrete `Localization.AtPrime 𝔮` rather
than an abstract `Sq` with `IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq 𝔮`, as in tag 00PK: the condition defining
the set has to be a predicate in `𝔮` alone, and it is invariant under the canonical isomorphism
`IsLocalization.algEquiv`, so nothing is lost.

Cohen–Macaulayness of a Noetherian local ring is `Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay A A` (tag 00NF),
that is `depth_{𝔪_A}(A) = dim A`, which is Definition 00N8 verbatim; that of the non-local
Noetherian fibre (Definition 00NC) is spelled out as a `∀` over its primes at the concrete
`Localization.AtPrime`, exactly as in the companion statements for tags 00ND and 00R9. "Equidimensional
of dimension `d`" is `TopologicalSpace.Equidimensional (PrimeSpectrum (𝔭.Fiber S))`, the
project's Definition 0058, together with `ringKrullDim (𝔭.Fiber S) = d`, again as in tag 00R9.
Neither `[IsNoetherianRing S]` nor finite type of the fibre over `κ(𝔭)` is assumed: both follow
from `Algebra.FiniteType R S`.

The hypothesis on the fibres is guarded by `Nontrivial (𝔭.Fiber S)`, that is by the fibre over
`𝔭` being nonempty, equivalently by `𝔭` lying in the image of `Spec S → Spec R`
(`PrimeSpectrum.nontrivial_iff_mem_rangeComap`). This is the source's hypothesis and not a
weakening of it: the source asks that all irreducible components of all fibres have dimension
`d`, which an empty fibre satisfies vacuously, while `ringKrullDim` of the zero ring is `⊥` and
not `d`. Dropping the guard would make the hypothesis unsatisfiable — hence the statement vacuous
— for every `R → S` whose `Spec` map is not surjective, `R = ℤ`, `S = ℚ` for instance.

Faithfulness to [StacksProject 00RA]:

1. No dead hypothesis. `f` occurs in the conclusion twice, as the locus and as the sequence.
   `[Algebra.FiniteType R S]` is the source's finite type hypothesis, and it is what makes the
   relative dimension finite and upper semicontinuous (Lemma 00QH), the step that turns a
   condition at one point into a condition on a neighbourhood. `hfib` is the source's hypothesis
   on the fibres, and it is the input of Lemma 00R9: a bound on the dimension of the fibres of
   `S/(f₁, …, f_i)` yields a regular sequence only because the fibres of `S` are Cohen–Macaulay
   and equidimensional. `d` occurs in `hfib` alone, as in the source, where it is a parameter of
   the hypothesis and not of the conclusion; what it carries is that all the fibres have one and
   the same dimension, which is what lets the dimension count at a point of the set be read on a
   neighbourhood of it.
2. The scalars and base are the source's. `S` is an `R`-algebra of finite type over `R`; the
   fibres are taken over `R` along `R → κ(𝔭)`; the elements `f₁, …, f_i` are elements of `S`
   itself; and the ring in which regularity is asserted is a quotient of a localization of `S`,
   an `S`-algebra, by the ideal generated by `𝔭` — not by a prime of `S`, and not over `κ(𝔭)`.
3. The canonical maps are pinned. `𝔭` is pinned as `𝔮.under R`, not merely assumed to lie under
   `𝔮`; `S_𝔮` is pinned as `Localization.AtPrime 𝔮` with its canonical `algebraMap S`; and the
   sequence whose regularity is asserted is the image `f.map (algebraMap S _)` of the source's
   own elements under the canonical `S → S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮`, not some sequence assumed to exist.
4. The instantiation is not degenerate. Take `R = k[t]`, `S = k[t][x, y]` and `d = 2`: every
   fibre is `κ(𝔭)[x, y]`, Cohen–Macaulay and equidimensional of dimension `2`, and nonempty, so
   `hfib` holds with the guard doing no work. For `f = [x, t * y]` one has
   `V(f) = V(x, t) ∪ V(x, y)`, and the set of the lemma is `D(t) ∩ V(x, y)`: at `𝔮 ⊇ (x, y)` with
   `t ∉ 𝔮` the images of `f` generate `(x, y)` in `S_𝔮/𝔭S_𝔮` and form a regular sequence, while
   at `𝔮 ⊇ (x, t)` the second image is `0`, which is not. So the set is a nonempty open subset of
   `V(f)` and is neither empty nor all of `V(f)`; in particular the statement is neither vacuous
   nor a triviality about `IsOpen Set.univ`.

